## How the DCO applies to this project

vibeforge-gate is **Apache-2.0** (see `LICENSE`). The DCO is this project's
contribution instrument, used **with explicit inbound = outbound terms**.

By adding a `Signed-off-by` line to a commit you certify the DCO above AND you
agree that your contribution is licensed **inbound = outbound under the Apache
License 2.0** — the project's `LICENSE`, which is Apache-2.0 §5's default in any
case. That includes the maintainer's right to license the contribution and, if
and when it happens, to **relicense or donate it to a foundation under
Apache-2.0**. You retain copyright to your work.

Why this is written down rather than assumed: that right is lost the moment one
contribution merges without it, and recovering it afterward needs unanimous
consent from every past contributor. A bare DCO without these explicit terms
would not secure it.

This mirrors the instrument used by the Sovereign Agent Control Plane, so
contributions can move between the two projects without a licensing mismatch.
**Note the scope difference:** SACP is deliberately on a C→A path toward CNCF
donation. This repository is not — it is Apache-2.0 with sign-off because that
is the right default for a package meant to be vendored into other people's
repositories, not because a foundation donation is planned for it.

## How to sign off

Add a `Signed-off-by` trailer to every commit, using your real name and an
email you can be reached at, matching your commit author identity:

    Signed-off-by: Jane Developer <jane@example.com>

Git adds this automatically with the `-s` flag:

    git commit -s -m "your message"

To sign off a branch of existing commits, rebase with `--signoff`, then
force-push:

    git rebase --signoff <base>
    git push --force-with-lease

## How it is enforced, honestly

This repository has no hosted CI. Sign-off is checked by the repository's own
merge bar — the `dco` check in `.vibeforge/gates.yaml` — which runs at pre-push
if you have installed the hooks:

    git config core.hooksPath .vibeforge/hooks

That is a **local hook, and local hooks are bypassable**: `git push --no-verify`
skips it, and a contributor who never sets `core.hooksPath` is never gated at
all. This project does not pretend otherwise — saying so plainly is the same
discipline the package itself preaches about SKIPped checks.

The actual enforcement is therefore **at review**: a maintainer verifies every
commit in a pull request carries a matching `Signed-off-by` before merging, and
a pull request that does not is fixed by signing off, never by waiving the
requirement. Run the check yourself before opening one:

    .vibeforge/gate.sh --only dco
